<p><strong>Why, climb batch 29.</strong> Not a new rule: the rule&rsquo;s answers stay, and two sentences follow what the batch fixed. Climb batch 29 made walk convert a float numeral where <code>RR64</code> is declared (row 943), and made two string literals of one text one object on both paths (row 945). So the sentence that named these two departures, and pointed to <code>interpreter.md</code> and <code>compiler.md</code> for them, is gone. Its example of a computed <code>RR64</code>, <code>0.25 + 0.25</code>, is now an expression of numerals alone, which the batch folds into one numeral before the run (change 70), so it no longer showed a computed value. The text now says &ldquo;a computed <code>RR64</code> 0.5&rdquo;. The sentence on two string literals joined by <code>||</code> now points to &ldquo;Numbers&rdquo;, which states the fold, and its citation of the Working Draft moved to the skill&rsquo;s list of sources. The orientation update made these changes, and its judge said to install them. The cold read found nothing to fix here.</p></div>
